    "craftName": "Hovercraft V2 Heavy 10T High-Force",
    "craftId": "hovercraft_v2",
    "craftClass": "Heavy",
    "description": "Heavy-class craft: 10,000 kg, 8.0 x 3.8 x 1.7 m — bigger, heavier and more powerful than the 7.5T Medium baseline. Redesigned 2026-07-23 from the historical 10T high-force test into a coherent class variant using the same target-derived methodology as the medium baseline.",
    "exportedUtc": "2026-07-23 (authored)",
    "units": "SI unless stated: kg, m, s, N, m/s, m/s2. Throttle/gain fields dimensionless.",
    "notes": "Derivations (rev 2 after hover-collapse fix): weight = 10,000 x 9.81 = 98,100 N. Hover 4 x 75 kN = 300 kN -> equilibrium 0.327, overdrive 3x -> 900 kN emergency (90 m/s2 surface-normal). hoverMaxCommand = 3 matches the overdrive rating so PD demand can unlock it (rev 1 capped demand at 1.0 -> emergency force unreachable -> belly scrape under downforce/curvature load). roofStabilizerMaxCommand 0.6 keeps roof pull-down (132 kN) well under hover authority. Main 300 kN = 3.06g, overdrive 1.5x -> 450 kN burst (4.6g). Brake 200 kN = 2.04g. Strafe usable 105 kN = 1.07g. Roof 55 kN/node. Power budget 1200: covers emergency hover at full overdrive (900) so protected hover is never starved. Aero CdA 3.2 -> drag-limited ~1,400 km/h; wing/GE ClA 12. Downward assist 0. Slower thruster response than medium (heavy hardware). The ORIGINAL unsaved 10T test state (500 kN on the legacy small hull, assist 25) remains preserved in Downloads/hovercraft_v2.json."
  },
